From: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] proxy: add Naive inbound and Chromium/Cronet outbound

Adapt sing-box Naive CONNECT authentication, padding and UoT to Xray.
Use the same cronet-go revision and Chromium 154 native libraries for
outbound HTTP/2 and HTTP/3, preserving the actual browser network stack.
Route tunneled TCP/UDP through Xray, retain outbound socket options and
dialer chains, and keep TLS verification mandatory in Cronet.

Add an HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3 inbound transport with per-stream
lifecycle handling. Match Xray's default private-target restrictions.
Naive outbound is opt-in with with_naive_outbound; with_musl selects
static OpenWrt archives. Inbound needs no native library.

Port source: sing-box dfb80349bf5779ec0a3f834c9ec2794345bff8f0
Cronet: 4d18a60dc3a8 (native libraries a1cafd93eb1f)
Sing-box-derived code is GPL-3.0-or-later; include its license.
Signed-off-by: coolsnowwolf <coolsnowwolf@gmail.com>

